n will change to an Eject icon, and once the drive has been dismounted, its icon will disappear from the desktop. After this, you can safely unplug the drive. On a Windows 7, 8 or 8.1 system, an icon reading \\\"Safely Remove Hardware and Eject Media\\\" will display on the system tray when a flash drive is inserted. To eject the drive, right-click that icon and select \\\"Eject USB Flash Drive\\\". A notification will appear when it's safe to remove the drive. If the utility notifies you that the flash drive is in use, close any files or applications that are running off the flash drive, and then try again.\", \"target\": \"any_unsupported_span_in_original_response\", \"visible_source_sentence_ids\": [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7], \"source_evidence_erased\": false}"}], "add_generation_prompt": true, "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": false}}
