n of the sinus cavities, while colds only involve inflammation of the mucous membranes.\\n\\nFever and fatigue: People with sinusitis may experience a higher fever and significant fatigue, while those with colds usually do not.\\n\\nHeadache: The headache associated with sinusitis is heavier and worsens when bending forward, whereas the headache caused by a cold is milder.\\n\\nNasal discharge: The nasal discharge in sinusitis is more yellowish and thicker than in a cold, where it may be clear. Additionally, the nasal congestion in sinusitis may persist for longer than in a cold.\", \"target\": \"any_unsupported_span_in_original_response\", \"visible_source_sentence_ids\": [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5], \"source_evidence_erased\": false}"}], "grammar": "root ::= \"{\" ws \"\\\"unsupported_probability\\\"\" ws \":\" ws probability ws \",\" ws \"\\\"source_sentence_id\\\"\" ws \":\" ws citation ws \"}\"\nprobability ::= \"0\" (\".\" [0-9]+)? | \"1\" (\".\" \"0\"+)?\ncitation ::= \"null\" | \"0\" | [1-9] [0-9]*\nws ::= [ \\t\\n\\r]*", "temperature": 0, "top_p": 1, "seed": 69058, "max_tokens": 96, "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": false}}
