ir candidate.\\n\u201cAsk yourself: why are they dropping historic money on Mississippi to flip it blue?\u201d Reeves said on social media. \u201cIt\u2019s because they know Brandon Presley will govern like a liberal democrat.\u201d\\nHowever, the big money boost from one of the top contributors to Democratic candidates around the country appears to signal the party's belief that they could successfully target Reeves in the upcoming 2024 election, potentially flipping the governor's position blue for the first time in almost 20 years.\", \"original_answer\": \"Democrat Brandon Presley is running a surprisingly competitive race for governor in the Republican stronghold of Mississippi, raising significant funds in his bid to flip the seat blue for the first time in nearly two decades. Presley has reportedly raised around $7.9 million this year, outpacing incumbent Republican Governor Tate Reeves, who has raised about $5.1 million. The Democratic Governors Association has also contributed $3 million to the race, signaling the party's belief in a potential upset in the 2024 election.\", \"target\": \"any_unsupported_span_in_original_response\", \"visible_source_sentence_ids\": [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8], \"source_evidence_erased\": false}"}], "grammar": "root ::= \"{\" ws \"\\\"unsupported_probability\\\"\" ws \":\" ws probability ws \",\" ws \"\\\"source_sentence_id\\\"\" ws \":\" ws citation ws \"}\"\nprobability ::= \"0\" (\".\" [0-9]+)? | \"1\" (\".\" \"0\"+)?\ncitation ::= \"null\" | \"0\" | [1-9] [0-9]*\nws ::= [ \\t\\n\\r]*", "temperature": 0, "top_p": 1, "seed": 69058, "max_tokens": 96, "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": false}}
