of what civil engineers do. They are responsible for conceiving, designing, building, supervising, operating, constructing, and maintaining infrastructure projects and systems in both the public and private sectors. This includes roads, buildings, airports, tunnels, dams, bridges, and water supply and sewage treatment systems.\\n\\nPassage 3 provides more details on the tasks that civil engineers typically perform. These include analyzing long-range plans, surveys, maps, and other data to plan projects, considering construction costs, government regulations, potential environmental hazards, and other factors when planning and risk assessment for a project.\\n\\nBased on these passages, it can be concluded that civil engineers play a critical role in designing, building, and maintaining various infrastructure projects and systems, including transportation systems, buildings, water supply systems, and waste management systems. They are involved in every stage of a project, from planning and design to construction and maintenance, and must consider a wide range of factors to ensure the safety, efficiency, and sustainability of the project.\", \"target\": \"any_unsupported_span_in_original_response\", \"visible_source_sentence_ids\": [0, 1, 2, 3, 4], \"source_evidence_erased\": false}"}], "grammar": "root ::= \"{\" ws \"\\\"unsupported_probability\\\"\" ws \":\" ws probability ws \",\" ws \"\\\"source_sentence_id\\\"\" ws \":\" ws citation ws \"}\"\nprobability ::= \"0\" (\".\" [0-9]+)? | \"1\" (\".\" \"0\"+)?\ncitation ::= \"null\" | \"0\" | [1-9] [0-9]*\nws ::= [ \\t\\n\\r]*", "temperature": 0, "top_p": 1, "seed": 69058, "max_tokens": 96, "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": false}}
